       "id": "CVE-2023-45803",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2023-45803: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-45803?s=redhat&n=python-pip&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in urllib3, an HTTP client library for Python. urllib3 doesn't remove the HTTP request body when an HTTP redirect response using status 301, 302, or 303, after changing the method in a request from one that could accept a request body such as `POST` to `GET`, as is required by HTTP RFCs. This issue requires a previously trusted service to become compromised in order to have an impact on confidentiality, therefore, the exploitability of this vulnerability is low. Additionally, many users aren't putting sensitive data in HTTP request bodies; if this is the case, this vulnerability isn't exploitable.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in urllib3, an HTTP client library for Python. urllib3 doesn't remove the HTTP request body when an HTTP redirect response using status 301, 302, or 303, after changing the method in a request from one that could accept a request body such as `POST` to `GET`, as is required by HTTP RFCs. This issue requires a previously trusted service to become compromised in order to have an impact on confidentiality, therefore, the exploitability of this vulnerability is low. Additionally, many users aren't putting sensitive data in HTTP request bodies; if this is the case, this vulnerability isn't exploitable.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                        |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/python-pip@9.0.3-24.el8?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                      |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.2] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                                                                           |\n"
