      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-116590",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-116590: Improper Validation of Array Index"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-116590?s=github&n=snappy-java&ns=org.xerial.snappy&t=maven&vr=%3C%3D1.1.10.8",
       "help": {
        "text": "### Impact\n`Snappy.arrayCopy(Object src, int offset, int byteLength, Object dest, int destOffset)` called a native `memcpy` without validating the ranges. A negative or oversized `byteLength` or offset read or wrote outside the arrays and crashed the JVM. `SnappyOutputStream.rawWrite` and `SnappyInputStream.rawRead`, and therefore the typed-array `write`/`read` methods, pass caller-supplied ranges to this method.\n\n### Patches\nFixed in 1.1.10.9 (#741). `Snappy.arrayCopy` checks both ranges before copying. The stream `read`/`write` methods validate offsets and lengths, and reject typed-array ranges whose byte size overflows `int`.\n\n### Workarounds\nValidate offsets and lengths before calling these methods.\n",
        "markdown": "> ### Impact\n`Snappy.arrayCopy(Object src, int offset, int byteLength, Object dest, int destOffset)` called a native `memcpy` without validating the ranges. A negative or oversized `byteLength` or offset read or wrote outside the arrays and crashed the JVM. `SnappyOutputStream.rawWrite` and `SnappyInputStream.rawRead`, and therefore the typed-array `write`/`read` methods, pass caller-supplied ranges to this method.\n\n### Patches\nFixed in 1.1.10.9 (#741). `Snappy.arrayCopy` checks both ranges before copying. The stream `read`/`write` methods validate offsets and lengths, and reject typed-array ranges whose byte size overflows `int`.\n\n### Workarounds\nValidate offsets and lengths before calling these methods.\n\n|                                                                                                                                 |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:maven/org.xerial.snappy/snappy-java@1.1.10.5  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <=1.1.10.8                                        |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.1.10.9                                          |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.9] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                    |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "affected_version": "<=1.1.10.8",
        "cvssV3": 5.9,
