       "id": "CVE-2021-31879",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2021-31879: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2021-31879?s=redhat&n=wget&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in wget. If wget sends an Authorization header as part of a query and receives an HTTP REDIRECT to a third party in return, the Authorization header will be forwarded as part of the redirected request. This issue creates a password leak, as the second server receives the password. The highest threat from this vulnerability is confidentiality.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in wget. If wget sends an Authorization header as part of a query and receives an HTTP REDIRECT to a third party in return, the Authorization header will be forwarded as part of the redirected request. This issue creates a password leak, as the second server receives the password. The highest threat from this vulnerability is confidentiality.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                      |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/wget@1.19.5-16.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                    |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                              |\n|[[CVSS Score 6.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                                                                         |\n"
