      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-102010",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-102010: Expired Pointer Dereference"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-102010?s=redhat&n=gcc&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in GCC. When an application calls the erase_if function on a binary heap priority queue in libstdc++, the library reallocates storage but fails to update its internal entry pointer. An attacker capable of triggering this operation can exploit this use-after-free condition, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS) via an application crash or potential memory corruption.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in GCC. When an application calls the erase_if function on a binary heap priority queue in libstdc++, the library reallocates storage but fails to update its internal entry pointer. An attacker capable of triggering this operation can exploit this use-after-free condition, leading to a Denial of Service (DoS) via an application crash or potential memory corruption.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/gcc@8.5.0-28.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                  |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                            |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.0] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H]]                                                                       |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
