       "id": "CVE-2026-44604",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-44604: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-44604?s=redhat&n=rpm&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A command injection vulnerability was discovered in the `rpmuncompress` utility of RPM. When extracting certain archive formats (ZIP, 7z, GEM) to a specified destination directory, the tool inserts the archive's top-level folder name into a shell command without properly sanitizing it. A specially crafted archive containing shell metacharacters in its folder name can execute arbitrary commands as the user running the extraction.\n",
        "markdown": "> A command injection vulnerability was discovered in the `rpmuncompress` utility of RPM. When extracting certain archive formats (ZIP, 7z, GEM) to a specified destination directory, the tool inserts the archive's top-level folder name into a shell command without properly sanitizing it. A specially crafted archive containing shell metacharacters in its folder name can execute arbitrary commands as the user running the extraction.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                     |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/rpm@4.14.3-32.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                   |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                             |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.0] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                        |\n"
