       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-95818?s=redhat&n=glibc&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in glibc, the GNU C Library. A local attacker can exploit a stack-based buffer overflow in the dynamic loader (ld.so) when a setuid/setgid (AT_SECURE) program's DT_RPATH or DT_RUNPATH begins with $ORIGIN followed by a null character or a slash. This vulnerability allows the attacker to crash the loader, leading to a denial of service, and potentially disclose limited process memory.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in glibc, the GNU C Library. A local attacker can exploit a stack-based buffer overflow in the dynamic loader (ld.so) when a setuid/setgid (AT_SECURE) program's DT_RPATH or DT_RUNPATH begins with $ORIGIN followed by a null character or a slash. This vulnerability allows the attacker to crash the loader, leading to a denial of service, and potentially disclose limited process memory.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                         |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/glibc@2.28-251.el8_10.40?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                       |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                 |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.0] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                            |\n"
