      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-95520",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-95520: Out-of-bounds Write"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-95520?s=redhat&n=rpm&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in rpm. Parsing a symlink entry in an untrusted RPM package whose declared RPMTAG_LONGFILESIZES value is 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF causes an integer overflow in iterReadArchiveNext() that shrinks a buffer allocation to one byte, after which the payload's independently-controlled cpio filesize field is used to write attacker-controlled data past the end of that allocation. This is reachable via rpm2cpio, rpm2archive, and rpm -qlvp on an  untrusted package.\n",
        "markdown": "> A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in rpm. Parsing a symlink entry in an untrusted RPM package whose declared RPMTAG_LONGFILESIZES value is 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF causes an integer overflow in iterReadArchiveNext() that shrinks a buffer allocation to one byte, after which the payload's independently-controlled cpio filesize field is used to write attacker-controlled data past the end of that allocation. This is reachable via rpm2cpio, rpm2archive, and rpm -qlvp on an  untrusted package.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                     |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/rpm@4.14.3-32.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                   |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                             |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.1] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H]]                                                                        |\n"
