      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-107161",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-107161: Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-107161?s=redhat&n=cyrus-sasl&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in Cyrus SASL. The add_to_challenge() function in the DIGEST-MD5 plugin computes the size of the buffer needed for a challenge/response field before DIGEST-MD5 quoting is applied, but does not recompute that size when quoting (escaping special characters) makes the value longer. The under-sized buffer is then passed to strcat(), causing a heap-based out-of-bounds write whose size depends on attacker-controlled input. A malicious or on-path DIGEST-MD5 (or HTTP Digest) server can trigger this flaw in a connecting client by supplying a crafted challenge field, such as realm or nonce, most likely resulting in a crash of the client application.\n",
        "markdown": "> A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in Cyrus SASL. The add_to_challenge() function in the DIGEST-MD5 plugin computes the size of the buffer needed for a challenge/response field before DIGEST-MD5 quoting is applied, but does not recompute that size when quoting (escaping special characters) makes the value longer. The under-sized buffer is then passed to strcat(), causing a heap-based out-of-bounds write whose size depends on attacker-controlled input. A malicious or on-path DIGEST-MD5 (or HTTP Digest) server can trigger this flaw in a connecting client by supplying a crafted challenge field, such as realm or nonce, most likely resulting in a crash of the client application.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                          |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/cyrus-sasl@2.1.27-6.el8_5?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                        |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                             |\n"
       },
