       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-33416: Expired Pointer Dereference"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-33416?s=redhat&n=libpng&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in libpng, a library used for processing PNG (Portable Network Graphics) image files. This vulnerability arises from improper memory management where a heap-allocated buffer is aliased between internal data structures. When specific functions are called, a freed memory region can still be referenced, leading to a use-after-free condition. An attacker could potentially exploit this to achieve arbitrary code execution or cause a denial of service.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libpng, a library used for processing PNG (Portable Network Graphics) image files. This vulnerability arises from improper memory management where a heap-allocated buffer is aliased between internal data structures. When specific functions are called, a freed memory region can still be referenced, leading to a use-after-free condition. An attacker could potentially exploit this to achieve arbitrary code execution or cause a denial of service.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                            |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/libpng@2%3A1.6.34-11.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                          |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                    |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                               |\n"
