       "id": "CVE-2026-34183",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-34183: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-34183?s=redhat&n=openssl&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSL's QUIC PATH_CHALLENGE handler. A remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by flooding a QUIC client or server with specially crafted PATH_CHALLENGE frames. This leads to unbounded memory allocation within the local QUIC stack, as the system continuously allocates PATH_RESPONSE frames without them being acknowledged. The primary consequence is a Denial of Service (DoS), causing the affected application to terminate abnormally due to memory exhaustion.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in OpenSSL's QUIC PATH_CHALLENGE handler. A remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by flooding a QUIC client or server with specially crafted PATH_CHALLENGE frames. This leads to unbounded memory allocation within the local QUIC stack, as the system continuously allocates PATH_RESPONSE frames without them being acknowledged. The primary consequence is a Denial of Service (DoS), causing the affected application to terminate abnormally due to memory exhaustion.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                            |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/openssl@1%3A1.1.1k-17.el8_6?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                          |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                    |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                               |\n"
