       "id": "CVE-2026-33636",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-33636: Buffer Underwrite ('Buffer Underflow')"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-33636?s=redhat&n=libpng&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in libpng. A remote attacker could exploit an out-of-bounds read and write vulnerability in the ARM/AArch64 Neon-optimized palette expansion path. This occurs when processing a final partial chunk of 8-bit paletted rows without verifying sufficient input pixels, leading to dereferencing pointers before the start of the row buffer and writing expanded pixel data to underflowed positions. This flaw can result in information disclosure and denial of service.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libpng. A remote attacker could exploit an out-of-bounds read and write vulnerability in the ARM/AArch64 Neon-optimized palette expansion path. This occurs when processing a final partial chunk of 8-bit paletted rows without verifying sufficient input pixels, leading to dereferencing pointers before the start of the row buffer and writing expanded pixel data to underflowed positions. This flaw can result in information disclosure and denial of service.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                            |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/libpng@2%3A1.6.34-11.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                          |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                    |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.6] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H]]                                                                               |\n"
