       "id": "CVE-2025-66293",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2025-66293: Out-of-bounds Read"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-66293?s=redhat&n=libpng&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "LIBPNG is a reference library for use in applications that read, create, and manipulate PNG (Portable Network Graphics) raster image files. Prior to 1.6.52, an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libpng's simplified API allows reading up to 1012 bytes beyond the png_sRGB_base[512] array when processing valid palette PNG images with partial transparency and gamma correction. The PNG files that trigger this vulnerability are valid per the PNG specification; the bug is in libpng's internal state management. Upgrade to libpng 1.6.52 or later.\n",
