       "id": "CVE-2026-19553",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-19553: Improper Certificate Validation"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-19553?s=redhat&n=python3&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in Python. When establishing secure connections using the SSLContext.wrap_bio() function with hostname checking enabled, the module fails to validate that a target server hostname is supplied. Because of this missing check, certificate hostname verification is silently skipped rather than triggering an error. A remote man-in-the-middle attacker could exploit this defect to spoof trusted endpoints and intercept or tamper with sensitive encrypted traffic.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in Python. When establishing secure connections using the SSLContext.wrap_bio() function with hostname checking enabled, the module fails to validate that a target server hostname is supplied. Because of this missing check, certificate hostname verification is silently skipped rather than triggering an error. A remote man-in-the-middle attacker could exploit this defect to spoof trusted endpoints and intercept or tamper with sensitive encrypted traffic.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                        |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/python3@3.6.8-78.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                      |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.4] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N]]                                                                           |\n"
