       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in Unbound, a Domain Name System (DNS) resolver. A remote attacker could trigger a heap overflow by sending specially crafted DNS reply packets. This occurs when Unbound attempts to encode multiple Name Server Identifier (NSID) or Extension Mechanisms for DNS (EDNS) Cookie options, or EDNS Padding options, and these options are enabled. Successful exploitation of this vulnerability could lead to a denial of service (DoS), making the Unbound service unavailable.\n",
