      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-42959",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-42959: Access of Uninitialized Pointer"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-42959?s=redhat&n=unbound&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in Unbound's DNSSEC validator when constructing chase-reply messages for validation. The code uses the wrong counter to calculate write offsets for ADDITIONAL section resource record sets. When a DNAME chain is combined with authority filtering, an uninitialized array slot is created that the validator later dereferences, causing an immediate process crash. Any application or infrastructure relying on Unbound for DNS resolution could be forced to exit unexpectedly, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in Unbound's DNSSEC validator when constructing chase-reply messages for validation. The code uses the wrong counter to calculate write offsets for ADDITIONAL section resource record sets. When a DNAME chain is combined with authority filtering, an uninitialized array slot is created that the validator later dereferences, causing an immediate process crash. Any application or infrastructure relying on Unbound for DNS resolution could be forced to exit unexpectedly, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                           |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/unbound@1.16.2-5.14.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                         |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                   |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                                              |\n"
