       "id": "CVE-2026-4424",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-4424: Out-of-bounds Read"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-4424?s=redhat&n=libarchive&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in libarchive. This heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability exists in the RAR archive processing logic due to improper validation of the LZSS sliding window size after transitions between compression methods. A remote attacker can exploit this by providing a specially crafted RAR archive, leading to the disclosure of sensitive heap memory information without requiring authentication or user interaction.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libarchive. This heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability exists in the RAR archive processing logic due to improper validation of the LZSS sliding window size after transitions between compression methods. A remote attacker can exploit this by providing a specially crafted RAR archive, leading to the disclosure of sensitive heap memory information without requiring authentication or user interaction.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                          |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/libarchive@3.3.3-7.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                        |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                                                                             |\n"
