      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-57585",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-57585"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-57585?s=pypa&n=msgpack&t=pypi&vr=%3C1.2.1",
       "help": {
        "text": "MessagePack is the serializer implementation for Python msgpack.org. Prior to 1.2.1, there is an Out-of-bounds read/crash on Unpacker reuse after a caught error, potentially leading to a DoS attack.  If the Unpacker is used repeatedly after an error occurs, the process may crash with a SEGV. This issue has been fixed in version 1.2.1.\n",
        "markdown": "> MessagePack is the serializer implementation for Python msgpack.org. Prior to 1.2.1, there is an Out-of-bounds read/crash on Unpacker reuse after a caught error, potentially leading to a DoS attack.  If the Unpacker is used repeatedly after an error occurs, the process may crash with a SEGV. This issue has been fixed in version 1.2.1.\n\n|                                                                                                       |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:pypi/msgpack@1.1.2  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <1.2.1                  |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.2.1                   |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                          |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "affected_version": "<1.2.1",
        "cvssV3": 7.5,
        "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
        "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
        "fixed_version": "1.2.1",
