      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-93451",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-93451: Off-by-one Error"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-93451?s=github&n=snappy-java&ns=org.xerial.snappy&t=maven&vr=%3C%3D1.1.10.8",
       "help": {
        "text": "### Impact\n`Snappy.uncompressCharArray`, `uncompressShortArray`, `uncompressIntArray`, `uncompressLongArray`, `uncompressFloatArray` and `uncompressDoubleArray` sized the result array by dividing the declared uncompressed byte length by the element size, but native code wrote the full byte length. If the declared length is not a multiple of the element size, up to 7 bytes are written past the end of the Java array, corrupting the heap.\n\n### Patches\nFixed in 1.1.10.9 ([#739](https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/pull/739)). These methods now reject uncompressed lengths that are not a multiple of the element size with `SnappyIOException`.\n\n### Workarounds\nCheck that `Snappy.uncompressedLength(input)` is a multiple of the element size before calling these methods.\n",
        "markdown": "> ### Impact\n`Snappy.uncompressCharArray`, `uncompressShortArray`, `uncompressIntArray`, `uncompressLongArray`, `uncompressFloatArray` and `uncompressDoubleArray` sized the result array by dividing the declared uncompressed byte length by the element size, but native code wrote the full byte length. If the declared length is not a multiple of the element size, up to 7 bytes are written past the end of the Java array, corrupting the heap.\n\n### Patches\nFixed in 1.1.10.9 ([#739](https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/pull/739)). These methods now reject uncompressed lengths that are not a multiple of the element size with `SnappyIOException`.\n\n### Workarounds\nCheck that `Snappy.uncompressedLength(input)` is a multiple of the element size before calling these methods.\n\n|                                                                                                                                 |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:maven/org.xerial.snappy/snappy-java@1.1.10.5  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <=1.1.10.8                                        |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.1.10.9                                          |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                                                    |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "affected_version": "<=1.1.10.8",
        "cvssV3": 7.5,
        "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
        "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
        "fixed_version": "1.1.10.9",
        "purls": [
         "pkg:maven/org.xerial.snappy/snappy-java@1.1.10.5"
        ],
        "security-severity": "7.5",
        "tags": [
         "HIGH"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: Use After Free"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964?s=github&n=msgpack&t=pypi&vr=%3C%3D1.2.0",
       "help": {
        "text": "### Impact\n\nIf the Unpacker is used repeatedly after an error occurs, the process may crash with a SEGV.\n\nIf the Unpacker is used repeatedly to unpack untrusted input from external sources, it may be vulnerable to a DoS attack.\n\n### Patches\n\nv1.2.1\n\n### Workarounds\n\nUsers should create a new Unpacker instead of reusing the same Unpacker after an error occurs.\n\nApplying the above patch can prevent SEGV, but reusing the Streaming Unpacker after it has encountered an error will not yield correct data. If an error occurs during Streaming Unpacking, the Stream and Streaming Unpacker should be discarded.\n\nTherefore, this is not just a workaround but the correct solution. The above patch only prevents crashes from incorrect usage.\n",
        "markdown": "> ### Impact\n\nIf the Unpacker is used repeatedly after an error occurs, the process may crash with a SEGV.\n\nIf the Unpacker is used repeatedly to unpack untrusted input from external sources, it may be vulnerable to a DoS attack.\n\n### Patches\n\nv1.2.1\n\n### Workarounds\n\nUsers should create a new Unpacker instead of reusing the same Unpacker after an error occurs.\n\nApplying the above patch can prevent SEGV, but reusing the Streaming Unpacker after it has encountered an error will not yield correct data. If an error occurs during Streaming Unpacking, the Stream and Streaming Unpacker should be discarded.\n\nTherefore, this is not just a workaround but the correct solution. The above patch only prevents crashes from incorrect usage.\n\n|                                                                                                       |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:pypi/msgpack@1.1.2  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <=1.2.0                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                  1.2.1                   |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.5] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H]]                          |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "affected_version": "<=1.2.0",
        "cvssV3": 7.5,
        "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
        "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
        "fixed_version": "1.2.1",
        "purls": [
         "pkg:pypi/msgpack@1.1.2"
        ],
        "security-severity": "7.5",
        "tags": [
         "HIGH"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "CVE-2026-103111",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-103111: Out-of-bounds Write"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-103111?s=redhat&n=pcre2&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in pcre2. When an application processes attacker-controlled regular expressions using certain Just-In-Time (JIT) compiler interfaces, an out-of-bounds write with arbitrary data can occur. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to achieve arbitrary code execution, corrupt memory, or cause a denial of service (DoS).\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in pcre2. When an application processes attacker-controlled regular expressions using certain Just-In-Time (JIT) compiler interfaces, an out-of-bounds write with arbitrary data can occur. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to achieve arbitrary code execution, corrupt memory, or cause a denial of service (DoS).\n\n|                                                                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/pcre2@10.32-3.el8_6?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                  |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                            |\n|[[CVSS Score 7.6] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:L]]                                                                       |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
