       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-75595?s=github&n=netty-handler&ns=io.netty&t=maven&vr=%3C%3D4.1.136.Final",
       "help": {
        "text": "### Summary\nA fragmented TLS ClientHello whose handshake header spans multiple records makes Netty silently fall back to the default SslContext; where per-SNI selection is the sole mTLS gate, an unauthenticated attacker can bypass the route's mTLS requirement.\n\n### Details\nIn `io.netty.handler.ssl.SslClientHelloHandler#decode` the guard that should wait for the 4-byte handshake header checks the wrong offset - it ignores the 5-byte record header that precedes it - and therefore never fires:\n\n```java\nif (handshakeLength == -1) {\n    if (readerIndex + 4 > endOffset) {\n        // Need more data to read HandshakeType and handshakeLength (4 bytes)\n        return;\n    }\n```\n\nWhen the first record's payload is < 4 bytes, `handshakeLength = in.getUnsignedMedium(readerIndex + SslUtils.SSL_RECORD_HEADER_LENGTH + 1);` leads to `IndexOutOfBoundsException `. That is caught by the generic `catch (Exception)` block, which calls `select(ctx, null)` - this is the default `SslContext`. Fallback to default on parse failure is a problem when per-SNI selection is the sole mTLS gate.\n\n### Impact\nSNI routing bypass. Escalates to an unauthenticated mTLS bypass only when:\n- mTLS is enforced solely via per-SNI SslContext (clientAuth=REQUIRE)\n- the default/fallback SslContext is permissive (clientAuth=NONE/OPTIONAL)\n- no secondary peer-certificate verification exists at the application layer.\n",
        "markdown": "> ### Summary\nA fragmented TLS ClientHello whose handshake header spans multiple records makes Netty silently fall back to the default SslContext; where per-SNI selection is the sole mTLS gate, an unauthenticated attacker can bypass the route's mTLS requirement.\n\n### Details\nIn `io.netty.handler.ssl.SslClientHelloHandler#decode` the guard that should wait for the 4-byte handshake header checks the wrong offset - it ignores the 5-byte record header that precedes it - and therefore never fires:\n\n```java\nif (handshakeLength == -1) {\n    if (readerIndex + 4 > endOffset) {\n        // Need more data to read HandshakeType and handshakeLength (4 bytes)\n        return;\n    }\n```\n\nWhen the first record's payload is < 4 bytes, `handshakeLength = in.getUnsignedMedium(readerIndex + SslUtils.SSL_RECORD_HEADER_LENGTH + 1);` leads to `IndexOutOfBoundsException `. That is caught by the generic `catch (Exception)` block, which calls `select(ctx, null)` - this is the default `SslContext`. Fallback to default on parse failure is a problem when per-SNI selection is the sole mTLS gate.\n\n### Impact\nSNI routing bypass. Escalates to an unauthenticated mTLS bypass only when:\n- mTLS is enforced solely via per-SNI SslContext (clientAuth=REQUIRE)\n- the default/fallback SslContext is permissive (clientAuth=NONE/OPTIONAL)\n- no secondary peer-certificate verification exists at the application layer.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                  |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:maven/io.netty/netty-handler@4.1.136.Final  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    <=4.1.136.Final                                 |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     4.1.137.Final                                   |\n|[[CVSS Score 9.1] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                                                  |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "affected_version": "<=4.1.136.Final",
        "cvssV3": 9.1,
        "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
        "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
        "fixed_version": "4.1.137.Final",
        "purls": [
         "pkg:maven/io.netty/netty-handler@4.1.136.Final"
        ],
        "security-severity": "9.1",
        "tags": [
         "CRITICAL"
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "id": "GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2: Improper Certificate Validation"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2?s=github&n=certifi&t=pypi&vr=%3E%3D2019.03.09%2C%3C2026.10.18",
       "help": {
        "text": "Certifi versions before 2026.10.18 include the `emSign ECC Root CA - G3` root certificate in their bundled CA store. Eight eMudhra intermediate CA certificates that chain to this root have compromised private keys and the CA has revoked them. \n\nAn attacker with one of the compromised keys can issue valid-looking certificates for any hostname. If the attacker is also on-path, they can intercept or modify TLS traffic from clients that trust the certifi bundle. Examples include `requests`, `urllib3` and `pip`, and the Python.org macOS installer.\n\nCertifi 2026.10.18 removed all emSign roots from the bundle. Certifi 2026.10.19 restored the emSign roots that are not affected. Upgrade to 2026.10.19 or later, and rebuild container images that vendor certifi.\n",
        "markdown": "> Certifi versions before 2026.10.18 include the `emSign ECC Root CA - G3` root certificate in their bundled CA store. Eight eMudhra intermediate CA certificates that chain to this root have compromised private keys and the CA has revoked them. \n\nAn attacker with one of the compromised keys can issue valid-looking certificates for any hostname. If the attacker is also on-path, they can intercept or modify TLS traffic from clients that trust the certifi bundle. Examples include `requests`, `urllib3` and `pip`, and the Python.org macOS installer.\n\nCertifi 2026.10.18 removed all emSign roots from the bundle. Certifi 2026.10.19 restored the emSign roots that are not affected. Upgrade to 2026.10.19 or later, and rebuild container images that vendor certifi.\n\n|                                                                                                                              |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:pypi/certifi@2026.6.17  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    >=2019.03.09,<2026.10.18    |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     2026.10.19                  |\n|[[CVSS Score 9.1] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                              |\n"
       },
       "properties": {
        "affected_version": ">=2019.03.09,<2026.10.18",
        "cvssV3": 9.1,
        "cvssV3_severity": "CRITICAL",
        "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N",
        "fixed_version": "2026.10.19",
        "purls": [
         "pkg:pypi/certifi@2026.6.17",
         "pkg:pypi/certifi@2026.7.22"
        ],
        "security-severity": "9.1",
        "tags": [
         "CRITICAL"
        ]
       }
      },
