       "id": "CVE-2026-81642",
       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-81642: Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-81642?s=redhat&n=unbound&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in Unbound's DNSSEC validator. A remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by controlling a malicious zone and sending a specially crafted DNSKEY record. This can lead to a heap buffer overflow, potentially resulting in a denial of service or remote code execution.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in Unbound's DNSSEC validator. A remote attacker can exploit this vulnerability by controlling a malicious zone and sending a specially crafted DNSKEY record. This can lead to a heap buffer overflow, potentially resulting in a denial of service or remote code execution.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                           |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:rpm/redhat/unbound@1.16.2-5.14.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=0                                                                         |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed                                                                   |\n|[[CVSS Score 9.8] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                              |\n"
