       "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
       "shortDescription": {
        "text": "CVE-2026-51302: Expired Pointer Dereference"
       },
       "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-51302?s=redhat&n=sqlite&ns=redhat&t=rpm&osn=redhatlinux&osv=8&vr=%3E%3D0",
       "help": {
        "text": "A flaw was found in SQLite. A use-after-free vulnerability in the expression evaluation logic, specifically within the sqlite3ReleaseTempReg and exprComputeOperands functions, allows a remote attacker to exploit the system. By supplying a malicious SQL statement, an attacker can cause a denial of service, leak sensitive information, or potentially execute arbitrary code.\n",
        "markdown": "> A flaw was found in SQLite. A use-after-free vulnerability in the expression evaluation logic, specifically within the sqlite3ReleaseTempReg and exprComputeOperands functions, allows a remote attacker to exploit the system. By supplying a malicious SQL statement, an attacker can cause a denial of service, leak sensitive information, or potentially execute arbitrary code.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                         |\n|Package                                                                         pkg:rpm/redhat/sqlite@3.26.0-21.el8_10?os_name=redhatlinux&os_version=8  |\n|Affected range                                                                  >=0                                                                      |\n|Fixed version                                                                   not fixed                                                                |\n|[[CVSS Score 10.0] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                                                                           |\n"
       },
